  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Empty panels are expected on a fresh clone\n\nNothing here has data until **Phase 2 — Observability** is implemented: the OTel SDK in each service, exporting over OTLP to `otel-collector:4317`. Until then Prometheus is running, is scraping, and is finding nothing to scrape — which looks identical to a broken dashboard and is not one.\n\n* What to build, and in what order → **`docs/learning-roadmap.md`**, Phase 2\n* Exact metric names, labels and the normative histogram buckets → **`docs/observability-specification.md`** §5\n* Check the pipeline itself right now → [Prometheus targets](/explore) · `curl localhost:9090/api/v1/targets` · `curl localhost:13133` (collector health)\n\nThe `taskflow-services` scrape job is a *fallback* `/metrics` path. Targets showing **down** before Phase 2 is the expected state, not a fault.\n\n> Once metrics arrive: click a spike on the latency panel below → the exemplar dot → the trace in Tempo → its logs in Loki → the flamegraph in Pyroscope. That chain is the whole point of the stack."
      },
      "transparent": false,
      "pluginVersion": "13.0.3",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "SLO status — the numbers you are actually held to",
      "id": 2,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Availability (selected range)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 99
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 99.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "text": {
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "100 * (1 - (\n  sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\",http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[$__range]))\n  /\n  sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__range]))\n))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "pluginVersion": "13.0.3",
      "description": "Objective 99.0% (`observability/slo/taskflow.yaml`). Non-5xx over total, computed over the dashboard's time range — widen the range to judge the SLO, narrow it to see an incident. 4xx is not an error here: a client sending bad input is the API working.",
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Latency SLI — under 250ms (selected range)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 95
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 99
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "text": {
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "100 * (\n  sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\",le=\"0.25\"}[$__range]))\n  /\n  sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__range]))\n)",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "pluginVersion": "13.0.3",
      "description": "Objective 95.0%. Note `le=\"0.25\"`, not 0.2: Prometheus can only evaluate a classic histogram at a bucket boundary, and NFR1's 200ms target falls between the 0.1 and 0.25 buckets. This is the conservative direction — it counts fewer requests as failures than a true 200ms cut. To measure exactly 200ms, add 0.2 to the bucket list in ALL FIVE implementations or the cross-language comparison breaks.",
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 8
      }
    },
